# Lathe — environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev, or set these in the Vercel project
# (Settings → Environment Variables). With NONE set, the app runs as the fully
# local, demo-seeded kiosk + dashboard (the Vercel preview default).
#
# Only `VITE_`-prefixed vars reach the browser bundle. The Supabase *secret*
# (service_role) key is NOT here — it's a server-only var set in Vercel and read
# by the /api functions. Never put it in this file or in git.

# --- Kiosk → live ingestion (leave VITE_KIOSK_KEY blank to stay local/demo) ---
# Scoped, ingest-only kiosk key (NOT a database key). The kiosk sends it as the
# X-Kiosk-Key header; the server resolves the kiosk by sha256 of this value.
# When set, lead capture POSTs to /api/leads and analytics events POST to
# /api/events (both offline-queued).
VITE_KIOSK_KEY=
# API base. Optional — defaults to same-origin "/api" (the functions deploy with
# the app). Only set this if the API lives on another origin (e.g. api.meetlathe.com).
# VITE_API_URL=

# --- Dashboard → Supabase (leave blank to run the dashboard as a local demo) ---
# When both are set, the dashboard requires a Supabase magic-link login and reads
# leads + analytics from the DB (RLS-scoped). The anon/publishable key is
# browser-safe (protected by Row Level Security).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Privacy notice shown on the lead form's consent line ---
# Defaults to https://meetlathe.com/privacy if unset. Point at the exhibitor's
# per-show privacy URL for a live event.
# VITE_PRIVACY_URL=

# ============================================================================
# SERVER-ONLY (set in Vercel, NOT in this file, NOT VITE_-prefixed):
#   SUPABASE_URL                = https://<project>.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   = <the Supabase SECRET / service_role key>
# Read only by app/api/*.ts (the ingestion functions). Never exposed to the browser.
# ============================================================================
